66
00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:49.090
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.344
Visal, tell me about someone resilient.

68
00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:58.297
My cousin. Despite the setback, she showed great resilience.

69
00:03:59.383 --> 00:04:00.547
What happened?

70
00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:06.706
She failed her exam. In spite of her disappointment, she studied again.

71
00:04:07.817 --> 00:04:08.853
And the result?

72
00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:13.366
Despite the pressure, she passed with a high score!

73
00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.884
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:20.003
Grammar focus: Despite and in spite of plus noun.

75
00:04:20.303 --> 00:04:21.513
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:22.217 --> 00:04:25.261
Despite the setback, she showed great resilience.

77
00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:28.974
In spite of her disappointment, she studied again.

78
00:04:29.883 --> 00:04:32.684
Despite feeling tired, he finished the race.

79
00:04:33.633 --> 00:04:39.931
After 'despite' or 'in spite of', use a noun or an -ing form, not a full clause. Never say 'despite of'.

80
00:04:40.683 --> 00:04:44.462
Be careful! Don't say: Despite of the setback, she kept going.

81
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.340
Say: Despite the setback, she kept going.

82
00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.777
Say 'despite' or 'in spite of', not 'despite of'.

83
00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:56.277
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:58.393
Rising Again.

85
00:04:58.693 --> 00:05:01.760
Resilience is the ability to bounce back from adversity.

86
00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:05.753
Despite setbacks, resilient people keep going.

87
00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:10.287
Grit and mental toughness help them persevere under pressure.

88
00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.867
A strong support system speeds up the recovery process.

89
00:05:15.867 --> 00:05:18.737
In spite of hard times, inner strength can grow.

90
00:05:19.833 --> 00:05:23.545
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:24.383 --> 00:05:26.987
Despite blank setback, she kept going.

92
00:05:27.287 --> 00:05:30.325
A, the. B, she had a. C, of the.

93
00:05:33.867 --> 00:05:35.437
The answer is A: the.

94
00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:39.477
To recover quickly after a problem is to blank back.

95
00:05:39.777 --> 00:05:42.652
A, bounce. B, come. C, turn.

96
00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.898
The answer is A: bounce.

97
00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.096
Courage and determination is blank.

98
00:05:51.396 --> 00:05:54.922
A, grit. B, adversity. C, stability.

99
00:05:58.467 --> 00:06:00.280
The answer is A: grit.

100
00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:04.990
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:08.952
Describe a challenge that helped you become more resilient.

102
00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.285
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:19.585 --> 00:06:29.703
When my family moved to a new city, I had no friends. Despite feeling lonely, I joined a club, and in spite of my shyness, I made good friends.

104
00:06:30.003 --> 00:06:31.816
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:32.717 --> 00:06:37.946
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and despite and in spite of plus noun.

106
00:06:38.246 --> 00:06:42.559
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

107
00:06:42.859 --> 00:06:45.569
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:45.869 --> 00:06:48.568
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

